---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';

const toc: [string, string][] = [
  ['principle', 'The principle'],
  ['not-allowed', 'What is not allowed'],
  ['health', 'Health, bodies and substances'],
  ['reporting', 'How to report'],
  ['enforcement', 'What happens next'],
  ['blocking', 'Blocking and controlling your feed'],
  ['appeals', 'Appeals'],
  ['contact', 'Contact'],
];
---

<Legal
  title="Community Guidelines"
  description="The standard for behaviour on ForgeFit's social features: what is not allowed, how to report objectionable content or abuse, and how we enforce it."
  updated="3 August 2026"
  version="1.0"
  toc={toc}
>
  <p>
    ForgeFit's social features are optional. If you use them (sharing workouts, commenting, appearing
    on leaderboards), these Guidelines apply. They form part of our
    <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a>.
  </p>

  <div class="callout">
    <p>
      <strong>ForgeFit has zero tolerance for objectionable content and abusive users.</strong>
      Content that breaches these Guidelines is removed, and the accounts responsible are suspended or
      permanently ejected. We action reports as quickly as possible, and generally within <strong>72 hours</strong>.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2 id="principle">The principle</h2>
  <p>
    This is a training app. People post their work, including sessions they are not proud of, weights
    that are modest, and bodies at every stage of change. The bar is simple: if it would make someone
    less likely to log their next session, it does not belong here.
  </p>

  <h2 id="not-allowed">What is not allowed</h2>

  <h3>Harassment and abuse</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Targeted insults, mockery, or pile-ons directed at another user.</li>
    <li>Body-shaming, including comments on someone's weight, size, or appearance.</li>
    <li>Ridiculing someone's numbers, technique, or progress.</li>
    <li>Threats of violence, intimidation, or stalking.</li>
    <li>Repeatedly contacting someone who has blocked you, or evading a block with a new account.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Hate speech and discrimination</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Content that attacks, demeans or dehumanises people on the basis of race, ethnicity, national
      origin, religion, disability, age, sex, gender identity, or sexual orientation.
    </li>
    <li>Slurs, hate symbols, or support for hateful organisations.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Sexual and graphic content</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Sexually explicit or pornographic content.</li>
    <li>Unsolicited sexual comments about another user or their photos.</li>
    <li>Gratuitously violent or gory content.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Any sexual content involving minors is reported to the relevant authorities and results
      in immediate, permanent termination.</strong>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Privacy and impersonation</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Posting another person's private information: address, phone number, workplace, or images of them without consent.</li>
    <li>Impersonating another person, a coach, a brand, or ForgeFit staff.</li>
    <li>Screenshotting and reposting another user's content to mock them.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Spam and manipulation</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Commercial solicitation, coaching sales, or supplement promotion.</li>
    <li>Links to external sites for the purpose of promotion.</li>
    <li>Fabricated lifts or manipulated data to place on leaderboards.</li>
    <li>Bulk or automated posting, or operating multiple accounts to inflate engagement.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Illegal activity</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Content promoting or facilitating illegal activity.</li>
    <li>Sale or sourcing of prescription drugs or controlled substances.</li>
    <li>Content that infringes copyright or trademark.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="health">Health, bodies and substances</h2>
  <p>
    Training communities have a specific set of failure modes. These are treated as seriously as any
    other breach:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>No promotion of disordered eating.</strong> That includes glorifying extreme restriction,
      purging, "what I eat in a day" content at dangerous calorie levels, or framing an eating disorder
      as discipline.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>No promotion of self-harm</strong> in any form, including training through injury framed
      as toughness.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>No sourcing, dosing advice, or promotion of anabolic steroids or other
      performance-enhancing drugs.</strong> Discussing your own history factually is not a breach;
      telling someone what to take, or where to get it, is.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>No presenting yourself as a medical professional</strong> or giving medical advice you
      are not qualified to give.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    If you are struggling with an eating disorder or thoughts of self-harm, please contact a
    professional service in your country. In Australia, the Butterfly Foundation (1800 33 4673) and
    Lifeline (13 11 14) can help.
  </p>

  <h2 id="reporting">How to report</h2>
  <p>You can report any content or user, and you do not need to interact with them to do it.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>In the app:</strong> use the report control on any workout post, comment, or user
      profile. Choose a reason and add detail if you want to.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>By email:</strong> <a href="mailto:safety@forgefit.fitness">safety@forgefit.fitness</a>,
      including the username involved and a screenshot if you have one.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Reports are confidential. We do not tell the reported user who reported them. Deliberately abusing
    the report system to harass someone is itself a breach of these Guidelines.
  </p>

  <h2 id="enforcement">What happens next</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Every report is reviewed and actioned as quickly as possible, and generally within 72 hours.</strong> Depending on severity, we
    will do one or more of the following:
  </p>
  <div class="table-scroll">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Severity</th><th>Action</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>Minor first breach</td>
          <td>Content removed, warning issued to the user</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Repeated breaches</td>
          <td>Content removed, social features suspended for a period</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Serious breach</td>
          <td>Immediate permanent termination of the account</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Illegal content</td>
          <td>Immediate removal, permanent termination, and referral to law enforcement</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>
    We may remove content and suspend accounts without prior notice where the content is clearly
    unlawful or presents a risk of harm. Users who are permanently ejected may not create new accounts.
  </p>

  <h2 id="blocking">Blocking and controlling your feed</h2>
  <p>You do not have to wait for us to act. At any time you can:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Block a user</strong> from their profile. They can no longer send you friend requests,
      see your activity, or interact with your workouts.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Hide any individual workout</strong> so it never appears in a feed.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Change your visibility</strong> in <em>Settings → Privacy &amp; Social</em>, including
      keeping everything private.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Leave social entirely.</strong> Social features are opt-in and can be switched off
      without affecting your training log.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Your progress photos, body measurements, Apple Health data and Ember conversations are never
    visible to other users under any setting.
  </p>

  <h2 id="appeals">Appeals</h2>
  <p>
    If your content was removed or your account was actioned and you believe we got it wrong, email
    <a href="mailto:safety@forgefit.fitness">safety@forgefit.fitness</a> with your username and what
    happened. We will review it and reply. We do not reinstate accounts terminated for illegal content
    or content involving minors.
  </p>

  <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Campbell Blair, trading as ForgeFit<br />
    ABN 14 278 891 663 &middot; Australia<br />
    Safety and abuse: <a href="mailto:safety@forgefit.fitness">safety@forgefit.fitness</a>
  </p>
</Legal>
